  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post-earthquake emergency debris removal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be removing 100,000 M3 of rubble from the streets, to restore full access to basic services for the affected populations in Harim district. This project will engage male and female workers from the affected population in a CFW scheme. The debris and rubble removal will be planned and documented by remote sensing technology which provides high-resolution satellite images comparing the situation pre- and post-earthquake, in collaboration with UNOSAT, to accurately identify the num</narrative>
  </description>
